  "type": "spr",
  "stem": "<p>A ball is thrown upward from the top of a building. The height \\(h\\), in feet, of the ball above the ground \\(t\\) seconds after it is thrown is given by \\(h(t) = -16t^2 + 64t + 192\\). How many seconds after it is thrown does the ball hit the ground?</p>",
