  "domain": "advanced",
  "skill": "Nonlinear functions",
  "difficulty": 3,
  "type": "spr",
  "stem": "<p>The height, in feet, of a rocket \\(t\\) seconds after launch is modeled by \\(h(t) = -16t^2 + 128t\\). The rocket is at a height of 240 feet twice: once on the way up and once on the way down. How many seconds after launch is the rocket at this height on the way down?</p>",
